	(footprint "xmitter:Adafruit_MCP4728_Breakout"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "373ba8f6-c979-42b8-9681-da14c6d1a262")
		(at 62.42 26.15)
		(descr "Adafruit MCP4728 4-channel 12-bit I2C DAC breakout. Board 25.4 x 17.78 mm (1.00 x 0.70 in), 4 corner mounting holes on 20.32 x 12.70 mm (0.80 x 0.50 in) spacing. Two 6-pin 0.1 in headers on the long edges: JP2 (top row = analog side) = GND / VA / VB / VC / VD / VCC left-to-right; JP1 (bottom row = I2C side) = VCC / GND / SCL / SDA / LDAC / RDY left-to-right. Because the xmitter:MCP4728 symbol only has 10 pins (VIN/GND/SCL/SDA/LDAC/RDY/VA/VB/VC/VD), the two physical VCC pads both get pad number '1' (share the VIN net) and the two physical GND pads both get pad number '2'. STEMMA QT connectors on the short edges are NOT represented -- I2C reaches the MCP4728 via daisy-chained STEMMA QT cable from the Si5351 breakout, so pads 3 (SCL) and 4 (SDA) here are intentionally left unrouted on the parent PCB. Verified against Adafruit datasheet pages 19-20 (schematic JP1/JP2 + fab print) 2026-07-09.")
		(tags "adafruit mcp4728 i2c dac breakout stemma qt")
